    {
      "number": 872,
      "title": "architecture: collapse the runtime to waves, projects, and tasks",
      "body": "## Usage\n\n```bash\ncargo build --bin lf\nlf wave start <wave>       # resident wave server, chat, projects, tasks\nlf chat                    # follow the wave's human thread\npython scripts/demo_sessions.py\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nThis collapses the runtime down to the three planning nouns the style guide already commits to — wave, project, task — and deletes everything that existed to support the old, speculative one. The `lfd` daemon is gone: its HTTP service, route surface, SQLite catalog with 60+ accreted migrations, queue reconciler, worktree fork machinery, provider/session token plumbing, and the `lfq` remote-exec door all go with it. What remains is a single `lf` binary with a resident wave server, a store rebuilt from one honest `001_initial.sql`, and a child-session layer that projects and tasks share instead of each growing their own executor.\n\nThe practical shape: a wave owns memory, cadence, chat, and project selection. A project is a bet with KRs, pursued by a durable child session. A task is concrete work under a project, run by the same primitives. Wave, project, and task each run one policy skill (`*_clarify` / `*_mutate` / `*_pursue`) rather than a three-tier phase ladder, and the flowloop driver/pass/run trio dissolves into that. Launch and control state on child sessions is now explicit, interrupting a stopped child is a no-op, and Wave Chat owns its own turn state and streams delegation visibly.\n\nThe Swift app follows the same cut. `RepoState`, `SessionState`, `WaveStore`, the multiplexer, the keyboard router, the terminal/Ghostty ownership, the bundled daemon manager, the credential socket, and the non-functional iOS shell are all removed. Loopflow.app is now Wave Chat plus a task workspace reading a live projection of the wave — `WaveWorkMap` and `TaskWorkspace` replace the caches, roadmap parser, and phantom run history.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Runtime**: `src/lfd/**`, `src/lfdb/**`, `src/lfq.rs`, `engine/fork.rs`, and `ops/{branches,combine,next,queue}.rs` deleted; `ops/{child,project,task,task_pm}.rs`, `child_session.rs`, `child_control.rs`, `project_session/`, `task/`, and `store/` added.\n- **Persistence**: registry identities are typed, the schema resets to a single initial migration, and project/task persistence is isolated behind `store/child_sessions`. Single-implementation traits are gone.\n- **PM**: Linear integration moves out of `lfd` to a top-level `pm/` module, task-scoped.\n- **Builtins/docs**: `LOOPFLOW.md`, flows, and skills teach the wave/project/task hierarchy; `docs/lfd.md` and the deploy/, docker/, and regression trees are removed.\n- **CI/packaging**: nightly docker-e2e, daily regression, and PyPI publish jobs dropped; release builds and ships only `lf`. Python is now test/script tooling, not a shipped client — `python/loopflow/models.py` and the DTO mirror it carried are deleted, with DTO fixtures re-cut for the new wire shape.",
      "files": [],
      "additions": 21396,
      "deletions": 61597,
      "changed_files": 511
